# Git Safety

This checkout is often dirty. Pre-existing modifications are protected.

## Forbidden unless the user names that exact operation

- `git reset --hard`
- `git clean -fd` / `git clean -fdx`
- `git checkout -- .` / `git restore .`
- `git stash` (including `-u`)
- force push to `main`/`master`

Do not discard, overwrite, or silently absorb unrelated work.

## Before any commit

Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git diff --stat`. Commit only intended files. Exclude secrets, generated junk, and unrelated dirty files.

## Checkpoints

Commit when the user asks, or when a coherent slice is ready and the user wants a recovery point: before risky architecture, migrations, dependency upgrades, ownership transfer, or release validation. Do not checkpoint after every tiny edit.

Message style: `feat(scope): why`, `fix(scope): why`, `chore(workflow): why`.

## Branch names

Prefer existing repo convention. Otherwise:

- `phase/<n>-<short-description>`
- `feature/<short-description>`
- `fix/<short-description>`
- `chore/<short-description>`
- parallel agents: `cursor/phase-<n>-<desc>` or `codex/phase-<n>-<desc>`

Do not proliferate branches for trivial edits on an already correct branch.
